{"title":"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Mathematical_Dexterity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Mathematical Dexterity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d49e13d3a684657a1c00de6dfc3e41250fb5f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} + i}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70cccfe7eef76892b86ead0a5c4f0a197e56d2d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\dfrac{-1 + i\\sqrt{3}}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2e92550cefae6e71b66ea8a86ac40ebcd6b9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = \\sqrt{-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> Find the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278a050cfc61472ef5ef809fec0576907c8108e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\cdot w^r = z^s.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in polar form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e7456466a27aa211cd14b0a9c9410da42714435.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} w &amp;= e^{i\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{6}}, \\\\ z &amp;= e^{i\\cdot\\frac{2\\pi}{3}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"75\" height=\"46\" />\nThe equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25ad6da8c97a8f4d0c3110100600cd4afb54c063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\cdot w^r = z^s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680bb54548d4a49b603164e0cce6da334c787ef0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} e^{i\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\cdot \\left(e^{i\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\right)^r &amp;= \\left(e^{i\\cdot\\frac{2\\pi}{3}}\\right)^s \\\\ e^{i\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}r\\right)} &amp;= e^{i\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}s\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}r &amp;= \\frac{2\\pi}{3}s+2\\pi k \\\\ 3+r &amp;= 4s+12k \\\\ 3+r &amp;= 4(s+3k). \\end{align*}\" width=\"203\" height=\"159\" />\nfor some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5ebbb98b521d7cd8344d72a49aba9fc8d556fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\leq 3+r\\leq 103$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/78239ab9e48e3db553979b17aa634aafcc6f31b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\mid 3+r,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> we conclude that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2d73bec8a696ada9087cf48e4a5bade32d8981.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 3+r &amp;\\in \\{4,8,12,\\ldots,100\\}, \\\\ s+3k &amp;\\in \\{1,2,3,\\ldots,25\\}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"214\" height=\"43\" />\nNote that the values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45eee91ff4a102b5fcfef83877ac5c532c1bf30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and the values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> have one-to-one correspondence.\n</p><p>We apply casework to the values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec39cfa30617e32f4f89e9a86d8601b8bb415d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644316ba373e9810a3f881906193068cbab36af6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k\\equiv0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /></li><p>\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e471252304e83f519cbd7645bfb4d28f3796053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279a83610a37e3f83bb8d2544695241ca8066834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40ca88589e76951dc27815c932fe106375a04b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\equiv0\\pmod{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d9c01a214955f96b174391be96b26abf545cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" /> </p><p>\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f0f77005458c547bbdf11773131fb59705395a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\cdot33=264$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> in this case.\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f96f26e3f03fb9aee8728a4a783db68ab5cfe58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k\\equiv1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /></li><p>\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e471252304e83f519cbd7645bfb4d28f3796053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279a83610a37e3f83bb8d2544695241ca8066834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/344e5361c8aa0f296104b58a21eb6aa7a52db93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\equiv1\\pmod{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d9c01a214955f96b174391be96b26abf545cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" /> </p><p>\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/7674e1e616cee9ca7152a8190ba4b6e4214aeff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\cdot34=306$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> in this case.\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d1653cbf5d52a00a88af71a643ce5bd3cd4cb41b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k\\equiv2\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /></li><p>\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e471252304e83f519cbd7645bfb4d28f3796053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+3k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279a83610a37e3f83bb8d2544695241ca8066834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea72bab964f2f4d53ec07543776d73e481688d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\equiv2\\pmod{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d9c01a214955f96b174391be96b26abf545cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" /> </p><p>\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f0f77005458c547bbdf11773131fb59705395a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\cdot33=264$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> in this case.\n</p></ol>\n<p>Together, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cdda8d6a7e711a1a15cb408e077b814d7252653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$264+306+264=\\boxed{834}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"196\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we recognize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/452a6a121949384e42e7d93c2fcb6b2a19c5c451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\operatorname{cis}(30^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d573d2e8b49bca35e212c39725fa2f12606e26f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\operatorname{cis}(120^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> because the cosine and sine sums of those angles give the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, respectively. By De Moivre's theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/03327e8d98c0e27f397211a315541adf092c1250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{cis}(\\theta)^n = \\operatorname{cis}(n\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />. When you multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, we can think of that as rotating the complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> counterclockwise in the complex plane. Therefore, by the equation we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8a1f27242beee15143223704057789715c18ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30r + 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b869ec48db32344a5362029a1b07b9bb4260759d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> land on the same angle.\n</p><p>This means that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523dd4e52636b2d72e29ea140616452216e43a3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30r + 90 \\equiv 120s \\pmod{360},\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" />\nwhich we can simplify to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/73745b5eb8d93273d9acddf1c91f43c1a1217cf0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r+3 \\equiv 4s \\pmod{12}.\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\nNotice that this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cycles by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for every value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. This is because once <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> hits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we get an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bd59024f5cb49b070ca9b0f8906499940c75e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> and the angle laps onto itself again. By a similar reasoning, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> laps itself every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, which is much easier to count. By listing the possible values out, we get the pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/08164c0d2ca54d49b9c550a8ce2e92e08fd796bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{cccccccc} (1,1) &amp; (5,2) &amp; (9,3) &amp; (13,1) &amp; (17,2) &amp; (21,3) &amp; \\ldots &amp; (97,1) \\\\ (1,4) &amp; (5,5) &amp; (9,6) &amp; (13,4) &amp; (17,5) &amp; (21,6) &amp; \\ldots &amp; (97,4) \\\\  (1,7) &amp; (5,8) &amp; (9,9) &amp; (13,7) &amp; (17,8) &amp; (21,9) &amp; \\ldots &amp; (97,7) \\\\ [-1ex] \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ (1,100) &amp; (5,98) &amp; (9,99) &amp; (13,100) &amp; (17,98) &amp; (21,99) &amp; \\ldots &amp; (97,100) \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"544\" height=\"104\" />\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> columns in total: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> values for the first column, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> for the second, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> for the third, and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for the fourth, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> for the fifth, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> for the sixth, etc. Therefore, this cycle repeats every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> columns and our total sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d990f992d896cd8088ac60ed899b25052baafe67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(34+33+33) \\cdot 8 + 34 = 100 \\cdot 8 + 34 = \\boxed{834}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"355\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tCpUJ7_j0U0?si=-Pn5Q2dAd0JBxwhy\">2022 AIME I #4</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Mathematical_Dexterity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Mathematical_Dexterity)\">Video Solution (Mathematical Dexterity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Mathematical Dexterity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XiEaCq5jf5s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XiEaCq5jf5s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qQ0TIhHuhnI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qQ0TIhHuhnI</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MJ_M-xvwHLk?t=933\">https://youtu.be/MJ_M-xvwHLk?t=933</a>\n</p><p>~ThePuzzlr\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/m1vg_DfHEX4\">https://youtu.be/m1vg_DfHEX4</a>\n</p><p>~AMC &amp; AIME Training\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-s